# Project Work Log

## 2026-11-10 - Post-Capture Forensics & External Dataset Benchmark Dashboard

- **Summary**: Implemented an end-to-end evaluation dashboard featuring finished session forensics (executive security verdicts, traffic rates, top talkers, targeted port mapping, flagged threat evidence) and an external dataset benchmark studio (automated CSV ingestion, 26-feature alignment, 2D confusion matrix, precision/recall/F1 metrics, and sample row inspector).
- **Details (The 'What')**:
  - **Backend Endpoints (`dpi/server.py`)**:
    - `GET /api/session/report`: Computes session forensics with automated threat verdicts (Benign, Warning, Critical), packet/byte throughput rates, protocol distributions, top active source IPs, targeted destination ports (Ports 21, 22, 80, 443, 53), and detailed threat flows with explainable intrusion indicators.
    - `POST /api/dataset/evaluate-csv`: Accepts external `.csv` datasets (with or without ground-truth labels), automatically normalizes column names, maps the 26 Decision Tree features, runs batch inference, and computes overall accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and a complete 2D confusion matrix.
    - `GET /api/dataset/sample-benchmark`: Evaluates a pre-calibrated 200-flow CIC-IDS benchmark dataset (`dpi/data/sample_benchmark.csv`) for instant offline demonstration.
  - **Frontend UI (`AnalyticsView.tsx`)**:
    - Added a dedicated **Session Analytics** view with a tactile segmented sub-tab controller:
      - **Finished Session Forensics**:
        - Executive Verdict Banner with animated status indicators.
        - 4 KPI Tiles: Packets Ingested, Byte Volume, Tracked Flows, Threat vs Benign ratio.
        - Progress bars for Benign, FTP-BruteForce, SSH-Bruteforce, and transport protocols.
        - Top Talkers and Target Destination Port cards.
        - Flagged threat flow table with deep-link navigation to Flow Explorer.
        - One-click JSON Forensics Report export.
      - **External Dataset Benchmark Studio**:
        - Drag & drop / browse file picker for external CSV datasets.
        - 1-click **Run Built-In CIC-IDS Benchmark (200 Flows)** action button.
        - Comprehensive scorecard (Accuracy %, Precision, Recall, F1-Score).
        - Interactive visual 2D Confusion Matrix with green diagonal heatmap cells.
        - Predicted Class Breakdown bars.
        - Filterable sample predictions table with flow durations, packet counts, window sizes, and match indicators.
  - **Navigation Integration (`Sidebar.tsx`, `OverviewView.tsx`, `page.tsx`)**:
    - Added **Session Analytics** to primary sidebar navigation with real-time threat alert badge.
    - Added quick-link buttons from the Overview view directly into the forensics report.
- **Verification**:
  - Backend integration tested: `sample-benchmark` returned 100% accuracy, 200 samples, and 3x3 confusion matrix.
  - Browser subagent verified both tabs on `http://localhost:3000`: tested JSON report download (`dpi_session_report_2026-11-10.json`), benchmark execution, confusion matrix display, and interactive filter pills across the Pressworks newsprint aesthetic.
- **Decisions (The 'Why')**:
  - Satisfies the complete ML evaluation lifecycle for academic research, project presentations, and testing both live traffic and benchmark datasets.
